  "contract": "Whether Cal.com branding is hidden for an event is a single derived rule, not a column read: it must be resolved through packages/features/profile/lib/hideBranding.ts, where resolveHideBranding (lines 35-45) makes the parent organization's hideBranding override the entity's own value, and where team ownership is resolved from team.hideBranding + team.parent.hideBranding while user ownership is resolved from owner.hideBranding + owner.profile.organization.hideBranding (lines 85-110). Every producer of an outbound message or of the Prisma projection feeding one \u2014 booking confirmation, workflow reminders, the pre-booking verification code, and the post-payment path \u2014 must call that resolver and must select the team/parent/profile-organization branding fields needed for it, instead of reading eventType.owner.hideBranding (or booking.user.hideBranding) directly or re-implementing the rule locally.",
  "defect_location": {
    "repo": "calcom/cal.com",
    "summary": "The booking page is correct because it routes through the resolver: apps/web/lib/team/[slug]/[type]/getServerSideProps.tsx, apps/web/server/lib/[user]/[type]/getServerSideProps.ts, apps/web/lib/d/[link]/[slug]/getServerSideProps.tsx and apps/web/lib/org/[orgSlug]/instant-meeting/team/[slug]/[type]/getServerSideProps.ts all consume shouldHideBrandingForTeamEvent/shouldHideBrandingForUserEvent from packages/features/profile/lib/hideBranding.ts, and packages/features/ee/payments/pages/payment.tsx:6,58-61 calls shouldHideBrandingForEvent. The messaging paths do not. (1) Reminder emails: packages/features/ee/workflows/api/scheduleEmailReminders.ts:519-535 defines its OWN shouldHideBranding, returning !!booking.eventType.team.hideBranding when a team exists and otherwise !!booking.user?.hideBranding \u2014 the literal team-vs-personal fork described in the report, with no organization inheritance \u2014 and it is applied at lines 246, 272, 300 and 433. (2) Confirmation: packages/features/bookings/lib/handleConfirmation.ts:458 and :471 pass hideBranding: !!updatedBookings[index].eventType?.owner?.hideBranding into workflow/reminder scheduling, and its own selects at :310 and :360 load only owner.hideBranding, so the team and organization values are never even fetched. (3) New and payment-initiated bookings: packages/features/bookings/lib/service/RegularBookingService.ts:2620, :2804 and :2819 all use !!eventType.owner?.hideBranding || !!platformClientId. The same owner-only read appears at packages/features/bookings/lib/handleBookingRequested.ts:103, packages/features/bookings/lib/handleCancelBooking.ts:464, packages/features/ee/round-robin/roundRobinManualReassignment.ts:669 and packages/features/ee/managed-event-types/reassignment/services/ManagedEventManualReassignmentService.ts:186. (4) The projections that make this unfixable at the call site: packages/features/bookings/lib/handleNewBooking/getEventTypesFromDB.ts:111, packages/features/bookings/lib/payment/getBooking.ts:40 (the paid-booking path), packages/features/bookings/repositories/BookingRepository.ts:462 and packages/features/bookings/lib/getBookingToDelete.ts:57 each select owner: { select: { hideBranding: true } } and nothing else; packages/features/ee/workflows/lib/getWorkflowReminders.ts:40 types the branding source as team: { parentId?: number; hideBranding: boolean } with selects at :170 and :201. (5) The verification code message: packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/auth/sendVerifyEmailCode.handler.ts:33-38 forwards only email/username/language/isVerifyingEmail to sendEmailVerificationByCode; packages/features/auth/lib/verifyEmail.ts:88-118 builds the code and calls sendEmailVerificationCode with no branding flag at all; packages/emails/auth-email-service.ts:31-33 constructs AttendeeVerifyEmail from packages/emails/templates/attendee-verify-email.ts, which was confirmed by bulk_search to contain no hideBranding \u2014 so that message is unconditionally branded. Contrast the compliant workflow services that already do it right: packages/features/ee/workflows/lib/service/WorkflowService.ts:11,133 and packages/features/ee/workflows/lib/service/EmailWorkflowService.ts:8,97,251-269 both import and await getHideBranding from the resolver, and packages/features/ee/teams/repositories/TeamRepository.ts:436-443 already exposes findTeamWithParentHideBranding, the parent-aware lookup the resolver depends on."
